quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  75,20,"(O disbelievers!) No, indeed! Instead, you love this transitory life,"
  75,21,and forsake the Hereafter.
  75,22,"Some faces shall be fresh and radiant on that Day,"
  75,23,looking at their Lord (unveiled).
  75,24,"And some faces will be scowling (in desperation) on that Day,"
  75,25,anticipating that they will be treated with a spine-crushing calamity.
  75,26,"No, indeed! When the soul reaches the throat (before it leaves),"
  75,27,and it is said: ‘Who is the healer (to save his life)?’
  75,28,And he (i.e. the dying person) knows this is the (time of) departure.
  75,29,And each leg clings to the other leg.
  75,30,On that day is the driving towards your Lord.
  75,31,"He neither confirmed (the truth) nor prayed,"
  75,32,"but persisted in denial and turned away,"
  75,33,"then, he went to his family boastfully."
  75,34,"So, woe to you (at the time of death)! Then, woe to you (in the grave)!"
  75,35,"Again, woe to you (on the Last Day)! Then, woe to you (in Hell)!"
  75,36,Does human being think he will be left aimless (without reckoning)?
  75,37,Was he not a fertilised egg (i.e. a zygote*) from a drop of seminal fluid?
  75,38,"Then he became a clinging mass (in the mother’s womb). Then He created (him in a bodily form with limbs) and proportioned (him) perfectly,"
  75,39,producing two genders from this (zygote): the male and the female.
  75,40,Is such (a Creator) not capable of reviving the dead?
  76,1,"Indeed, there has been a span of time upon human being when he was not something worth mentioning."
  76,2,"Indeed, We created human being from a drop of mingled fluid (i.e. a zygote*) that We may examine him (from stage to stage). Then, We endowed him with hearing (and) seeing."
  76,3,"Indeed, We have shown him the way, whether (he chooses to be) grateful or ungrateful."
  76,4,"Indeed, We have prepared for the disbelievers chains, iron collars and a blazing Fire."
  76,5,The virtuous will have a (pure) drink mixed with camphor.
